A||||11||saleenfiero||Wet tire look||||1||
Z||000000||saleenfiero||06-17-2001||12:56 PM||||With my new rims and tires, I'm wondering, should I put that black wet tire look stuff on them?  They look good, and I don't want them to succumb to the browning effect I heard some of those products do.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||06-17-2001||01:08 PM||||now that my car is 4-5 different colors i don't go about shining and polishing everything (sometimes i'll clean the wheels though). i think i was using black magic tire wet before. now that i've stopped they pretty much just look like dull tires. don't really notice any browning.||||reg||1
Z||000002||XDrewX||06-17-2001||01:32 PM||||I used the black magic clear gel......it turned my tires rust looking and i never could get them black again.<P>currently i use mequiares gold class endurance.  it is a white liquid, and it comes with an applicator.  if your tires are very clean when you put this on the shine will even last through rain.  i have had the shine last 3 weeks before.  but i didnt drive much and we had no rain.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||06-17-2001||01:34 PM||||I use the Meguires Gel. Really last a long time and easy to apply. Smells like grape Kool-Aid too. I like it. Good stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000004||CoolBlue87GT||06-17-2001||02:04 PM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by saleenfiero:<BR><B>With my new rims and tires, I'm wondering, should I put that black wet tire </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I perfer the wet look.  For car shows it's a must.  I've tried a few types, the last being Meguiars 'Eundrance high gloss'.<P>It was okay, it's a gel and comes with an foam applicator.  <P>(Oh yes,  grape Cool-Aid,  I was wondering what that smelled like. Thanks,  been a long time since I'd tried Cool-Aid)<P>I also have had good luck with Eagle One 'Wet tire shine' It's in a spray bottle.<P>Another is TurtleWax "Wet'n Black", spray also. You get more product for less $$  - I like that !<P>So far I like the spray better, as I like to cover the tread at shows, and is hard to do with a gel.  - all though the gel appears to last longer.  I might use both - what the heck.<P>I usually spray a rag, then apply to the tire to keep the over spray down.  The tread side I shoot with the spray directly.<P>Those foam spray tire shine really don't do the same trick.   I think you get less, and pay more for those.<P>I'll send two pic's  one w/out ,  one with.<P>None of these products have turned brown - although, when washing the car, with another bucket & mit, I do wash down the tires w/Joy<BR>dish soap.  (just on the Tires & wheels)<BR>I use another type soap for the paint.<P>Cuts the brake dust w/out hurting the clearcoat on the wheels.<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Del4more.jpg">    <BR>        Above w/out     below with<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Del5more.jpg">    <BR>[img]<BR>Good luck with your Fiero. <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CoolBlue87GT.gif">   <p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 06-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||mikemrq||06-17-2001||06:40 PM||||I use Meguires gel, i put it on with a sponge brush-nice shine||||reg||1
Z||000006||prtzlboy||06-17-2001||10:28 PM||||the reason most people have trouble with their tires turning brown after using these products is typically that the tire is not clean enough before they apply it.  It will trap the dirt underneath the coat of whatever product you use.  Think of this stuff as a wax for your tires.  Just THOROUGHLY clean your tires before you put it on and you should be fine.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||06-18-2001||01:04 PM||||its a matter of taste, personaly I like my tires just plain old dull clean black, not looking like they just got a coat of black laquer. I just use a brush and something like 409 or Fantastic. also it dont mess up the rims.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||06-18-2001||03:32 PM||||i use 2001 protectant (lime green spray bottle).. it doesn't contain Alcohol which accelerates the browing and it doesn't make them shiney or like polised rice. they just look clean and new all the time. <P><BR>oh yeah if you use a thick coating  like armour all or most gels they will sling on to the cars finish and leave oil blemishes... the 2001 doesn't. <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex2004||06-18-2001||04:16 PM||||I use the armorall tire foam, it works really well, leaves a good shine, and last a long time, beads water off the tires like wax, and it doesn't seem to fade our tires either.<P>Alex...||||reg||1
Z||000010||Leadfoot||06-18-2001||07:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by XDrewX:<BR><B>I used the black magic clear gel......it turned my tires rust looking and i never could get them black again.<P>currently i use mequiares gold class endurance.  it is a white liquid, and it comes with an applicator.  if your tires are very clean when you put this on the shine will even last through rain.  i have had the shine last 3 weeks before.  but i didnt drive much and we had no rain.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Had the same problem, you might want to use a product I believe is called tire bleech.  It not only made my tires black again but it whitened my lettering as well.  Don't get it on your aluminum rims though.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fierowrecker||06-18-2001||09:26 PM||||Hey Saleen!<BR>Start by cleaning your tires with Westlies bleach white, let them dry and see if you like that look...<BR>If you want the wet look, try armor all first to see if you like how it picks up the dust...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
